card.statement:
Let $t_1, \ldots, t_s$ be local parameters at a non-singular point $P \in X$. Then there
exists a unique embedding

\begin{equation}
\whp : \DD \hookrightarrow \HD ,
\end{equation}

such that the following diagram is commutative:

\begin{equation*}
\begin{CD}
\DD \times A @>>> A \\
@V{\whp \times \pi}VV @VV{\pi}V\\
\HD \times R @>>> R
\end{CD}
\end{equation*}
